==English==

===Etymology===
From Greek [[διοπτρικός]]. Compare [[diopter]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/daɪˈɒptrɪk/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|obsolete}} Pertaining to a [[diopter]].
# Acting as a medium for sight; making use of refraction (of lenses, etc.).
# {{label|en|obsolete}} Capable of being seen through.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|in the plural}} The branch of [[optics]] concerned with [[refraction]].
# A dioptric [[telescope]].

===Derived terms===
* {{l|en|dioptrical}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|en|diprotic}}

